            <ArticleTitle>Vagally mediated multivessel coronary artery spasm during coronary angiography.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>423-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We report on a case of multivessel coronary artery spasm preceded by vagal signs and symptoms, which resolved after administration of atropine. This supports that the spasm was triggered by endogenous acetylcholine.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
